{"name":"Cucumber","hex":"#006400","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cucumber","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vine in the gourd family, Cucumis sativus.","The edible fruit of this plant, having a green rind and crisp white flesh."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cucumber"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cucumber","blocks":[{"text":"The cucumber is a widely-cultivated creeping vine plant in the family Cucurbitaceae that bears cylindrical to spherical fruits, used as culinary vegetables. Considered an annual plant, there are three main types: slicing, pickling, and seedless."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/ARS_cucumber.jpg/330px-ARS_cucumber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucumber","wikidata":"Q23425"},{"title":"Cucumber (British TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Cucumber is a 2015 British comedy drama television series created by Russell T Davies and aired on Channel 4. Exploring 21st-century gay life, the series focuses on middle-aged Henry Best. Following a disastrous date night with his boyfriend of nine years, Lance Sullivan, Henry's old life shatters. He embarks on a new life with unfamiliar rules."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/dd/Cucumber_titles.png/330px-Cucumber_titles.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucumber_(British_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q5192414"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Cucumber_BNC.jpg/500px-Cucumber_BNC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Cucumber_BNC.jpg/1280px-Cucumber_BNC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Cucumber_BNC.jpg/500p